{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610081400-old-west-saloon-effort-xhigh","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-sonnet-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"The Silver Nugget Saloon: silver-camp false-front frontier saloon","rationale":"Second pass, improve-not-redesign. KEPT from pass 1: the seven-bay front (corner | window 3 | pier 2 | door 2 | pier 2 | window 3 | corner), the dark-oak frame over a stone_bricks body, the 3-deep porch and balcony shelf, piers 1 block proud below the cornice, recessed glass and doors (carved by not placing the front stone), the sign board with its cap slab in the balcony rail, batwing trapdoors, benches, barrels, hay, hitching rails, lanterns and cacti. FIXED where it read flat or unfinished: (1) The side faces were flush glass in a flat stone wall. They are now a two-layer wall: the outer layer is left open at each window cell and the glass sits 1 block back. Sills are 2 deep, with dark lintel belts at y=5 and y=10, log posts at z=0/5/10/15 rising through the parapet, and a coping slab, so the long street-visible flank gets the same shadow-line depth as the front. (2) The spruce plank band that wrapped the whole base is replaced by a stone_bricks plinth under the walls. Spruce is kept for the boardwalk, balcony deck, sign and interior floors only, so the pale wood reads as the working surface. (3) The porch gets stone footings under its four posts, dark end beams that close the frame under the deck, and knee-brace brackets (inverted dark_oak_stairs) beside every post. That reads as carpentry and frames the stepped entrance. (4) The crown is chamfered with stone_brick_stairs so the stepped top reads as a cut silhouette against the sky. The wing coping slabs and side/back parapet coping stay, which keeps the false front the tallest element. (5) Inside, hanging lanterns glow through the ground and upper windows and the batwing doors, so the ground floor invites you in. (6) The wall sign blocks are now on the street face of the sign board (facing north) so the lettering faces the street; they were on the balcony side before. Block ids use 1.20.1 names (hay_block). Palette hierarchy is unchanged: stone_bricks dominant, dark_oak frame, spruce accent, with glass_pane and lantern for light. Repeated bays are identical left and right, and no noise textures or extra clutter were added."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:stone_brick_slab","minecraft:stone_brick_stairs","minecraft:dark_oak_planks","minecraft:dark_oak_log","minecraft:dark_oak_slab","minecraft:dark_oak_stairs","minecraft:dark_oak_fence","minecraft:dark_oak_door","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:spruce_trapdoor","minecraft:spruce_wall_sign","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:lantern","minecraft:barrel","minecraft:hay_block","minecraft:potted_cactus","minecraft:red_wall_banner"]},"placements":[{"op":"fill","from":[0,0,-3],"to":[13,0,15],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,1,0],"to":[13,1,15],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,1,-3],"to":[13,1,-1],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[2,1,2],"to":[11,1,14],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[6,1,0],"to":[7,1,1],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[5,1,-3],"to":[8,1,-3],"block":"minecraft:spruce_stairs","state":{"facing":"south","half":"bottom","shape":"straight"}},{"op":"voxel","pos":[0,1,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"voxel","pos":[4,1,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"voxel","pos":[9,1,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"voxel","pos":[13,1,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,6,-3],"to":[13,6,-1],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[2,6,2],"to":[11,6,14],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,6,0],"to":[13,6,1],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[6,6